  "caption": "Quinn woke up stuck looking left, and shoulder checks became whole-body turns.\n\nA wry neck usually comes from an irritated neck joint plus protective muscle guarding. It can feel dramatic, but it's usually harmless and often settles within days.\n\nWhat often helps: gentle movement within comfort a few times an hour, heat for comfort, turning your whole body for a couple of days, breaking up long still positions and leaving heavy overhead jobs for later. Soft collars can make it linger, and forcing or cracking it yourself can stir it up.\n\nGet it assessed with fever, a recent knock, arm pins and needles or weakness, severe unrelenting pain, or if it's not clearly better by day three or four or keeps coming back.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
